#29701
"The Heart of the White Fortress"
"In the center of the room is a beautiful circular water fountain.  A sculpture
of a naked elven woman stands in the center of the fountain elegantly pouring
crystal-clear water into the fountain.  Both the woman and the fountain appear
to be carved out of the same marble as the fortress.  The ceiling and floor
glow with a soft hum, illuminating the entire room leaving no shadows.  No
tiles or seams of any kind can be seen in the marble work.  Perhaps this was
all carved out of a single piece of marble.  There is a hallway leading south,
deeper into the fortress, and one leading back north towards the entrance.
"
""
